/* MdCheckbox — https://m3.material.io/components/checkbox/specs
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §6 row 1, §8.5 "Comportamento observado".
 * Figma: `checkbox / android / deselected` inside `Row Calmo` 109:952 et al —
 * a 24x24 instance with 3dp padding around an 18x18 box, r2, 2px stroke.
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * GEOMETRY (1 USS px = 1 dp = 1 Figma pt, §1.2)
 *   root       48x48   touch target (V2's 24dp instance is well under the 48dp
 *                      minimum every other interactive component here honors)
 *   container  40x40   pill-radius state-layer disc, M3's ripple size
 *   box        18x18   r2, 2px `outline` border when unchecked,
 *                      0 border + `primary` fill when checked
 *   check      16px    Material Symbols `check`, `on-primary`
 *
 * WHY r2 IS A LITERAL AND NOT A SHAPE TOKEN
 *   The shape scale (§3.5) is the BRAND radius ladder: 8/10/12/14/16/20/24/pill.
 *   2dp is an M3 component constant for this one control and appears nowhere in
 *   V2's ladder, so adding a rung for it would pollute the vocabulary the
 *   designer retunes. TokenDisciplineTests only governs colors; sizes are
 *   literals throughout the library (MdChip's 32dp, MdIconButton's 40dp).
 *
 * WHY THE CHECK IS `display` -TOGGLED, NOT COLOR-TOGGLED
 *   An always-present glyph tinted to transparent would need a literal color.
 *   Toggling `display` costs nothing (the box is fixed-size, so nothing reflows)
 *   and keeps every color in this file a token.
 *
 * THE BOX IS A FLEX CENTERER, NOT A SIZED TEXT ELEMENT
 *   Same reason MvNumberedList's marker is: TextCore's line box for a 16px face
 *   is taller than the glyph, so a fixed-height text element fights its own
 *   vertical alignment. A flex box centering a free-sized MdIcon is stable.
 */

.md-checkbox {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* Unity's default theme dims disabled elements to 0.5; every interactive
 * component here opts out and paints its own disabled colors instead. */
.md-checkbox:disabled {
    opacity: 1;
}

.md-checkbox__container {
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-full);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    /* Required by the state-layer contract: the layer must follow the disc. */
    overflow: hidden;
}

.md-checkbox__box {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-outline);
    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);
}

.md-checkbox__check {
    font-size: 16px;
    display: none;
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-primary);
}

/* ---- Checked ---- */

.md-checkbox--checked .md-checkbox__box {
    border-width: 0;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

.md-checkbox--checked .md-checkbox__check {
    display: flex;
}

/* ---- Interaction states ----
 * The ripple takes the color of whatever the control currently IS: neutral while
 * unchecked, `primary` once checked — M3's own rule. */

.md-checkbox .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
}
.md-checkbox--checked .md-state-layer {
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
}

.md-checkbox:hover .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-hover-opacity);
}
.md-checkbox:focus .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-focus-opacity);
}
.md-checkbox:active .md-state-layer {
    opacity: var(--md-sys-state-pressed-opacity);
}

/* ---- Disabled ---- */

.md-checkbox:disabled .md-checkbox__box {
    border-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-content);
}
.md-checkbox--checked:disabled .md-checkbox__box {
    border-width: 0;
    background-color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-container);
}
.md-checkbox:disabled .md-checkbox__check {
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-disabled-content);
}
